, {"text": " "}, {"text": "indication"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "method"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "re-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "evaluated."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11423", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pre-induction assessment", "runs": [{"text": "Pre-induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessment"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11424", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Health care providers should assess the cervix (using the bishop score) to determine the likelihood of success and to select the appropriate method of induction.", "runs": [{"text": "Health care providers should assess the cervix (using the bishop score) to determine the likelihood of success and to select the appropriate method of induction."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11425", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "The bishop score should be documented.", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "bishop"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "score"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "documented."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11426", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Care providers need to consider that induction of women with an unfavorable cervix is associated with a higher failure rate and increased rate of operative deliveries.", "runs": [{"text": "Care providers need to consider that induction of women with an unfavorable cervix is associated with a higher failure rate and increased rate of operative deliveries."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11428", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Post-dates induction", "runs": [{"text": "Post-dates"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11429", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Women should be offered induction of labour between 41+0 and 42+0 weeks as this intervention may reduce perinatal mortality and meconium aspiration syndrome without increasing the Caesarean section rate", "runs": [{"text": "Women should be offered induction of labour between 41+0 and 42+0 weeks as this intervention may reduce"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "perinatal mortality and meconium aspiration syndrome without increasing the Caesarean section rate"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11430", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Women who chose to delay induction >41+0 weeks should undergo twice-weekly assessment for fetal wellbeing", "runs": [{"text": "Women"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "delay"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": ">41+0"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weeks"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "undergo"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "twice-weekly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "assessment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fetal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "wellbeing"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11432", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Options for Cervical Ripening/Induction: Unfavorable Cervix", "runs": [{"text": "Options"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cervical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Ripening/Induction:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Unfavorable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Cervix"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11433", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Intracervical Foley catheters are acceptable agents that are safe both in the setting of a vaginal birth after Caesarean section and in the outpatient setting", "runs": [{"text": "Intracervical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Foley"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "catheters"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "acceptable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "agents"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "safe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "setting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "birth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after Caesarean section and in the outpatient setting"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11434", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Double lumen catheters may be considered a second-line alternative", "runs": [{"text": "Double"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "lumen"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "catheters"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "considered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "second-line"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "alternative"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11436", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Pharmacological Treatment", "runs": [{"text": "Pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Treatment"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11437", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: misoprostol (PO) 25µg 2hourly for 24hours or Misoprostol (PV) 25µg 6hourly for 24hours can be considered a safe and effective agent for labour induction with intact membranes and on an inpatient basis.", "runs": [{"text": "A: ", "bold": true}, {"text": "misoprostol (PO) 25µg 2hourly for 24hours or Misoprostol (PV) 25µg 6hourly for 24hours can be considered a safe and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effective agent for labour induction with intact membranes and on an inpatient basis."}]}, {"id": "body-11438-textbox1-00001", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Note:", "runs": [{"text": "Note", "bold": true}, {"text": ":"}]}, {"id": "body-11438-textbox1-00002", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Misoprostol should not be used in the setting of vaginal birth after Caesarean section due to the increased risk of uterine rupture.", "runs": [{"text": "Misoprostol"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "not"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "used"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "setting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "birth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Caesarean"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "section"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "increased"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "risk"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of uterine rupture."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1418"}}, {"id": "body-11438-textbox1-00003", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Oxytocin should be started no earlier than 4hours after the last dose of misoprostol.", "runs": [{"text": "Oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "started"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "no"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "earlier"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "4hours"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "last"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "misoprostol."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1418"}}, {"id": "body-11439", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Options for induction with a favorable cervix", "runs": [{"text": "Options"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "favorable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cervix"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11440", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Amniotomy should be reserved for women with a favorable cervix. Care should be given in the case of unengaged presentation because there is a risk of cord prolapse.", "runs": [{"text": "Amniotomy"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "reserved"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "women"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "favorable"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cervix."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Care"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "given"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "case"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "unengaged presentation because there is a risk of cord prolapse."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11441", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "After amniotomy, oxytocin should be commenced early in order to establish labour. • In the setting of ruptured membranes at term, oxytocin should be considered before expectant management.", "runs": [{"text": "After amniotomy, oxytocin should be commenced early in order to establish labour. • In the setting of ruptured"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "membranes at term, oxytocin should be considered before expectant management."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11442", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Women positive for group B streptococcus (GBS) should be started on oxytocin as early as possible after ruptured membranes in order to establish labour within 24 hours.", "runs": [{"text": "Women"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "positive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "group"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "B"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "streptococcus"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(GBS)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "should"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "started"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "early"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "as"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "possible"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ruptured membranes in order to establish labour within 24 hours."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11443", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Both high- and low-dose oxytocin may be considered within a hospital protocol.", "runs": [{"text": "Both"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "high-"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "low-dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "be"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "considered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "within"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hospital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "protocol."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11444", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Because of the various concentrations, oxytocin infusion rates should always be recorded in mU/min rather than mL/hr.", "runs": [{"text": "Because of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the various concentrations,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "oxytocin infusion rates should always be recorded in mU/min rather"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "than "}, {"text": "mL/hr."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11445", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Oxytocin induction maybe considered in the hospital setting of vaginal birth after Caesarean section.", "runs": [{"text": "Oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "maybe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "considered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "hospital"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "setting"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "vaginal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "birth"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "after"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Caesarean"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "section."}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11446", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "For induction of labour use: Oxytocin IV, the dose will depend on parity", "runs": [{"text": "For"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "induction"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "labour"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "use:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "IV,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dose"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "will"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "depend"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "on"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "parity"}], "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1419"}}, {"id": "body-11447", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Primigravida", "runs": [{"text": "Primigravida"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-11448", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "A: oxytocin (IV) 5IU in 500mls of 0.9% sodium chloride the initial dose should be 8-10drops/Minute, the titration may be gradually increased at intervals not shorter than 20 minutes and increments of not more than 5drops/minute, until a contraction pattern similar to that of normal labour is established. The recommended maximum rate is 40d/m.", "runs": [{"text": "A:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "oxytocin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IV)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "5IU"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "500mls"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "0.9% sodium"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chloride"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "ini